                <pb facs="0736" n="722" xml:id="pg722"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Garcia, Peruvian
                        minister, to Mr. Seward, Secretary of
                        State</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Translation.—Extract.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <dateline><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Clarendon Hotel</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">New York</hi></placeName>, <date
                        calendar="gregorian" when="1868-05-08"><hi rendition="#italic">May</hi> 8,
                        1868</date>.</dateline>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: If, in order to your acceding to the
                    intimation I have hinted at, it were necessary to promise positively that the
                    vessels which go from the United States shall proceed on the route to Peru
                    without attacking or provoking attacks from other nations, without any
                    exception, nor to cause injury nor to offer threats to their possessions, I hold
                    in pledge to the United States the honor of the Peruvian government from this
                    moment.</p>
                <p>I avail myself, with satisfaction of this opportunity to renew to your excellency
                    the assurances of the high respect and esteem with which I subscribe myself your
                    very obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>JOSÉ ANTONIO G. Y GARCIA.</signed>
                </closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>His Excellency <hi rendition="#small-caps">Wm. H. Seward</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c., Washington.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
